  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Camping Côté Mer is a 3-star campsite in Mandelieu-la-Napoule, in the bay of Cannes between the Estérel and the Tanneron, 600 m from La Raguette beach according to its website. It offers mobile homes (Classic, Comfort and Premium ranges), a heated outdoor pool, a snack-pizzeria and a boules court. It is run by Homair (Marvilla Parks brand) and open from 9 April to 3 October 2027.</p>

      <h2>Dogs</h2>
      <p>The campsite's page on Homair says "one dog allowed (not 1st and 2nd category)", as a paid service; the Mandelieu-la-Napoule tourist office lists the site as "pets accepted, with a fee". The Marvilla Parks group also states that all its campsites welcome dogs, on pitches and in mobile homes. Only one vehicle is allowed inside the campsite, others park in the outside car park. Gas and charcoal barbecues are banned, only electric ones are allowed.</p>
      <p><strong>Check before you go:</strong> the amount of the dog fee (€6/day in Classic/Comfort and €8/day in Premium appeared in the earlier version of this page, but I did not find them on the pages read), any size limit applied in rentals (not published on the pages read) and the areas of the campsite closed to dogs, which are not detailed. The phone number above is the one in the site's footer; it replaces an old number that could not be found again.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The site places the campsite 600 m from La Raguette beach and a few minutes from the centre of Mandelieu and the port of La Napoule. Beach rules for dogs should be checked with the town.</p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>campingcotemer.com (home page and services), the campsite's Homair page, Marvilla Parks' "dog-friendly camping" page and the Mandelieu-la-Napoule tourist office listing, read on 08/11/2026.</p>
